Subject: Cantor Caller Stimulus Argument Grounding Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 202d0be8-4977-4800-add4-0cb5ec681300
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Caller_Stimulus_Argument_Grounding.sop

& [Problem] is identity-bearing attribution drift
  + a schema-valid enum can be forced into a learned call even when the caller named a different subject
  + current host code trusts Needle's optional validation account and does not independently compare arguments to caller text
  + high learned confidence coexisted with thirteen caller-subject mismatches

& [Decision] is literal host grounding
  + check every string argument against only the preserved caller stimulus
  + use NFKC casefold whitespace normalization with complete phrase boundaries
  + reject the whole selection before semantic execution when any field is absent
  + disclose only offending field names

& [WhyNow] follows observed proof
  + route-only calibration produced a reproducible fault without external effect
  + the correction directly realizes the Honesty and Security identity-boundary role in ordinary inspectable code
  + the gate complements rather than replaces typed schema and confidence policy

& [Deferred] remains explicit
  + structured declared-field parsing can later enforce exact field-to-value attribution
  + synonyms and semantic equivalence require a different evidence and authority model
  + literal presence cannot establish truth, consent, or safe external effects
